      "settings": {
        "kicker": "A GUIDE FROM THE MAISON",
        "title": "Ring Sizing Guide",
        "intro": "<p>A ring should settle on the hand without argument. Firm at the base of the finger, free enough to turn. These are the three ways to find your size.</p>",
        "chart_title": "Size chart",
        "notes_title": "A few things to know",
        "notes_text": "<p>Measure at the end of the day. Fingers are smaller in the morning, fuller at night. The size you wear most of the day is the one that should fit.</p><p>Skip the cold. Fingers contract in low temperatures. A morning measurement in winter will read a full size small.</p><p>Between two numbers, choose the larger one. A ring that is slightly loose will wear comfortably for decades. A ring that is slightly tight becomes a problem.</p><p>The dominant hand is often a half size larger. Worth measuring both.</p><p>Wide bands sit heavier. If the band is wider than six millimeters, consider going up half a size.</p><p>Still unsure? Write to the concierge. We will help you find your size, quietly.</p>",
        "concierge_label": "Concierge:",
